sonora (0.3.8) unstable; urgency=low

  * Meters and spectrum are synchronised with the sound automatically: results
    carry the stream time of the audio and are released when the audio sink
    has played up to it (the analysis runs 1.3 s / 2.3 s for the true-peak
    branch ahead of the sound, which is why ~2200 ms had to be entered).
    The delay setting is now a fine-tuning offset, -500 ... 4000 ms.
  * Fix: the time display and seek bar used the pipeline position, which is
    the maximum over all sinks and was ~2.3 s ahead of the sound because of the
    unthrottled sink of the true-peak branch; the audio sink's position is
    used now.

 -- Your Name <you@example.com>  Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100

