sonora (0.3.6) unstable; urgency=low

  * Fix: tracks of a cue sheet. The old code ended a track with SEGMENT_DONE,
    which GStreamer posts when the data reaches the sink (up to ~1.2 s before
    the sound is played), so tracks were cut short and chained through the
    album within seconds; the last track inherited the stop position of the
    previous one and ended immediately. Tracks now end with a normal EOS
    (when the sound really ends) and the stop position is always set. The
    exact cause of the reported hang when starting a cue-only playlist could
    not be reproduced; the start no longer depends on a bus message (the
    pre-roll is polled, with a timeout) and playback stops when 8 tracks end
    within a second.
  * Resuming at the same position after a sound-service change uses the same
    polling.
  * Cue sheets with full Windows paths are resolved by file name.
  * SONORA_DEBUG=1 prints player events.

 -- Your Name <you@example.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:00:00 +0100

sonora (0.3.5) unstable; urgency=low

  * CUE sheet support: a .cue (with FLAC/APE/WV/WAV/MP3 ... image) is expanded
    into one playlist entry per track, with title/artist/album/year/genre from
    the sheet; folders skip audio files that a cue sheet already covers.
  * Player: playing a part of a file, tracks of one image switch without
    re-opening the file; time and seeking are relative to the track.

